WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.910
- Hey guys, this novel
coronavirus pandemic

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.880
has truly affected all
of us across the globe,

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.680
but one of the hardest hit communities

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.090
has been healthcare frontline workers.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:14.170
This means doctors, nurses,
CMAs, respiratory therapists,

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:17.370
technicians, custodial
staff, and so many more.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.210
Today I'd like to take a
focus and celebrate doctors,

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.770
in memory of those who've
laid down their lives

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.650
in the battle against COVID-19.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.960
I sat down, and I interviewed
over 100 physicians

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.520
to get their take, their experiences,

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.660
and learn their perspectives
about the coronavirus.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.870
Know that all the revenue
generated from this video,

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:40.400
AdSense, donations, and even
merch sales, link down below,

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.700
are all going to the CDC Foundation

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.310
to help continue this
battle against COVID-19.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.530
The first question I asked these doctors,

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.850
what do you think is not
getting enough attention?

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.700
- I wish there was more credit
and awareness being given

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.380
to other members of the healthcare teams,

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.530
aside from just the
doctors and the nurses.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.230
- Techs, transporters,
housekeeping, kitchen staff,

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.550
valets, operators.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.161
- X-ray, laboratory, radiology
techs, EMT, janitorial staff.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:05.240
- Cafeteria workers, the
respiratory therapists, the nurses,

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.446
and everyone else here on the frontline is

00:01:06.446 --> 00:01:08.340
towards our abilities to do our jobs.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.690
- The number of doctors and
healthcare professionals

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:12.050
out there who have gotten seriously ill,

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.110
even lost their lives
fighting this disease.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:17.520
- Some healthcare workers have
been disciplined for speaking

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.300
up about the lack of personal
protective equipment.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.810
- Testing is an area we need
a huge amount of focus on

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:24.210
and attention on in the UK.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.160
- We need antibody tests.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.140
We need to know who has immunity.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.870
- In many communities, the small number

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.060
of cases being reported
is simply a reflection

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.000
of lack of testing.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.010
- How coronavirus is and will
affect certain communities,

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.290
our homeless community,
our community of people

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.210
with special needs.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.570
- The domestic abuse and domestic
violence that is happening

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.560
during a pandemic with
victims being in the same home

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.430
as perpetrators for longer periods of time

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.417
in this quarantine.

00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:48.020
- We've limited and cut the number

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.500
of visits a woman can
have before she delivers.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.680
- Visitors, family, really
no one is allowed to be

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.830
at the bedside when you're
infected with COVID.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:56.550
- If you look closely, you will see that

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.440
there are young people,
who are otherwise well,

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:00.990
who can get seriously ill.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.460
- We can't really see the emotional toll

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.950
that the outbreak has on us.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.190
- The effect that this is all having

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:07.800
on our mental health and well-being.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.340
- Mental health problems don't stop

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.010
just because we are having an
infectious-disease pandemic.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.330
- I've had patients who haven't been able

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:17.010
to get cancer surgery, who've
had significant heart problems

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:19.300
and not been able to get them worked up.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.260
- If people who now feel sick from cancer

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.300
are now discouraged
from going to hospitals

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.860
because all the attention
now is on COVID-19,

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.610
then we're gonna miss
some of those patients.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.470
- Right now we're postponing
all the non-urgent cases,

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:31.660
and when things are lifted,

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.550
we're gonna see everyone
come back all at once.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:36.060
- How is one supposed to
date in this point in time?

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.500
Are we just supposed to get to know people

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.820
by Zoom and FaceTime?

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.310
- Yeah, virtual dating is a thing now.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.890
For my next question, I
asked, what does it mean

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.830
for you to be a doctor now?

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:49.300
- It means a 30-minute
decontamination routine before I get

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:52.230
to hug my kids every time I
come home from the hospital.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.180
- Practicing medicine
during this pandemic means

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.900
what it always means,
protecting the vulnerable.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.714
- This is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity

00:02:58.714 --> 00:03:03.110
to boldly fulfill my oath
and desire to save lives.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.230
- The COVID-19 pandemic has me in a place

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.370
where I have never felt more
connected to my profession.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.980
- I have an opportunity to step
up and really honor my oath.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.980
- I really feel like it's a
privilege for me to be able

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.890
to practice medicine during the pandemic.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.230
It allows me to serve my community

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.828
when my community needs me most.

00:03:16.828 --> 00:03:18.760
- I'm old enough to have
lived through the early years

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.200
of the AIDS epidemic, and
it had a similar feeling.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.430
You knew you were in the middle

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.790
of something incredibly important.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:26.448
- My mother gave me a magnet
a long time ago that said,

00:03:26.448 --> 00:03:28.407
"Not all heroes wear capes.

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:30.000
"Some of them wear stethoscopes."

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.450
- I'm not running away from it.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:32.670
I'm running toward it.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.090
- We're ready, we signed up
for this, we took an oath.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.380
- It's a privilege to be
a part of the solution.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.360
- It's an honor to care for
patients and their families and

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.140
to help navigate them through
these very challenging times.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.120
- Medicine is a calling and a vocation.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.790
I've never viewed it as a job.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.030
- This isn't a job.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:49.950
This is a calling.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.240
- I couldn't agree more.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.210
Next I asked, how have you
been personally affected

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.520
by the coronavirus?

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.720
- When we put a breathing
tube in for a patient,

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.681
which we have to do for
almost every surgery,

00:03:59.681 --> 00:04:02.540
we're really exposed to everything that's

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.250
in that patient's mouth
or throat or airway.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.600
It's like looking down
the barrel of a gun.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.980
- I'll be moving out of our house soon

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.250
and into some place that's
closer to the hospital

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.130
and where I won't risk
infecting my own family.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.360
- Should I move out, should
I isolate within the home?

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.940
- I haven't seen my mom or
my dad or any family members

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.150
in the last few weeks.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.700
- I have some sick family members.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.960
I don't know when I'll see them next.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.140
- I wasn't able to kiss my wife
on our anniversary this year

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.350
because of coronavirus.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.310
- My beautiful wife and I
are about to bring new life

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:31.250
into this world, and with
that comes fear, worry,

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.083
and anxiety.

00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:33.430
- Both of my daughters work with me here

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:34.560
at the Cleveland clinic.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.210
I'm worried for the family,
but we're gonna do this.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.940
- My entire family lives and practices

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.870
a self-care survival
simile, and when I read

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.960
in the news that 2,027
physicians, as of yesterday,

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.450
have contracted the virus
and many have died from it,

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.840
it gave me chills.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.410
- I recently got sick with a lot

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.830
of the features of COVID-19.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.640
Without testing, I've
got no way of knowing

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:54.530
if I had it for sure.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:56.250
I don't know if I'll be infected again.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.810
I don't know if I'm going
to infect my patients.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:04:59.850
- I did get corona.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.300
I was actually sick for
two weeks, had pneumonia,

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.690
and it was probably the
worst health experience

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:05.748
that I have ever been through.

00:05:05.748 --> 00:05:08.196
- I developed a fever and a
lot of the COVID symptoms.

00:05:08.196 --> 00:05:10.240
When I ended up in the emergency room,

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.270
all I could think about
was when I recover,

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:14.520
will this make me immune so
I can get back out there?

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.830
- For the first time ever, lately,

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.310
I've been having the sense of uneasiness

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:20.480
as I drive into work.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:24.360
- I've personally seen a lot
of death that I don't know

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.690
if residency could ever prepare you for.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.740
- Because our pain clinics
closed down last week,

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.830
and before I'll be transitioning
to telemedicine soon,

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.310
there's still a gap where
I will be unemployed

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.530
as a pain management fellow,

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.100
and that leaves me financially unstable.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.520
- So I'm still paying rent,
overhead, staff, supplies,

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.030
all of the above with basically no income.

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:44.230
- I'm a physician on O'ahu,
and it's challenging caring

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:47.250
for my neighbor island patients
on Maui and the Big island.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:49.460
- Hydroxychloroquine has
been getting a lot of press

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.600
during this pandemic, and the availability

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:55.390
of this medication has been
a big concern for myself

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:56.780
and for my patients.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:59.410
- I've been forced to
delay important heartbeat

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:02.010
and heart rhythm procedures
for several of my patients.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:05.090
- I lost childcare, so
my toddler keeps barging

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.430
into all of my appointments,

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.710
and that's probably a HIPAA violation.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:10.800
- Hey, I can relate.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.080
Bear walks into some of
my patient visits too.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.050
Next I asked, how can we help from home?

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:16.883
- Believe it or not,

00:06:16.883 --> 00:06:20.210
not everyone is taking
social distancing seriously.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.120
- The virus doesn't spread on its own.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:25.790
People spread the virus,
so you are on the frontline

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:26.690
in this pandemic.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.870
- Even small indulgences,
like going to a park

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.270
around other people, can
have huge consequences

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.900
that you don't even feel in the moment.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.278
- Treat every outside contact

00:06:34.278 --> 00:06:36.997
as something potentially
infected, no matter how healthy

00:06:36.997 --> 00:06:39.240
or safe someone or something looks.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.850
- This thing does not
care what you look like,

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:43.470
how much money you have,
or how wealthy you are,

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:44.690
so you have to stay home.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:45.523
- No cheating.

00:06:45.523 --> 00:06:47.840
I know it gets really
boring at home sometimes,

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.870
and all you want to do is
just be with your friend just

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.140
for a minute, but please,
for our sake, stay home.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.180
- Stay home.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.370
That's how you fight the virus.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.010
- Get comfortable, and stay there.

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:57.920
Netflix and chill.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:58.940
YouTube and thrill.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.420
- Please, please, please stay home.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.660
Help us help you.

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:04.780
- Help me help you.

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:07.610
- Stay hydrated, get some
sleep, eat healthy, don't smoke,

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.650
and please do some exercise
while you're at home.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.300
- Here's my prescription for you.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:12.230
Stay home.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:13.790
- We are not stuck at home.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:14.780
We are safe at home.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:17.280
- Safe at home, not stuck at home.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.070
And please treat everyone with kindness.

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:22.100
- Everyone knows someone
who is putting their life

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:24.710
at risk by working during
these difficult times.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.700
Just send them a thank you.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.590
- Continue sending positive
vibes and continue reaching out

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.260
to those who are in their support system.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.093
We need their help.

00:07:32.093 --> 00:07:33.130
- And just be kind to each other.

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:34.430
Everyone's having a hard time.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.710
- Physical distancing is crucial,

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:39.650
but it should not cause social isolation.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:42.120
- Call or FaceTime your
friends, your family,

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.140
your significant others.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.040
- The virus mainly infects
through mucus membranes

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:47.670
of the eyes, nose and mouth,
so even if we wear gloves

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:49.380
and we wear masks, if we touch our face,

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.650
we can still get infected.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.390
- Washing your hands, and
no I'm not just talking like

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.610
oh, wash, wash, wash, and you're done.

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:57.630
I'm talking a full 20 seconds.

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:59.310
- Wash your hands.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.410
- Wash your hands multiple
times throughout the day.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:02.790
- Really diligent hand washing.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:03.830
- Wash your hands.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.590
- And as I say to my five year
old, don't pick your nose.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.380
- Be wary of the browsers and the pickers

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.517
at the grocery store.

00:08:09.517 --> 00:08:11.610
You know I'm talking about,
those people that are picking

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:12.990
up avocados and putting them right back.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:15.320
- By being very careful
of your internet hygiene

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:18.560
because spreading false
information can be deadly.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.200
- Everyone has a role
to play in making sure

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.240
that we spread correct information.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:25.300
- Stop spreading
misinformation on social media.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.800
I think this is very important.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.890
- Just following credible media outlets.

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:30.080
Don't give in to the hysteria.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.300
- The top thing on my mind, is remembering

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:35.170
to stay flexible and
lean into uncertainty.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:37.700
- Have those difficult
end-of-life discussions.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.880
You will feel at peace knowing
your loved one's wishes,

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:43.480
whether the time comes
tomorrow or a decade from now.

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:45.410
- Ask neighbors to put
up a red piece of paper

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.630
in their window if they
need assistance immediately.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:50.610
A yellow piece means I need
help, but not urgently.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.410
And green means things are okay.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:54.700
- And please know that when the scientists

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.840
are saying these things,
we're not saying them

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.680
because we're out to get you.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:01.020
We're saying them because
we care about you.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:01.853
- That's right.

00:09:01.853 --> 00:09:03.260
We're on team you.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:05.820
All right, my final question,
what gives you hope?

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.130
- It gives me goosebumps when I think

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:08.940
about what you see around you.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.700
- The doctors, nurses, social workers,

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:14.220
respiratory therapists,
environmental services.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.692
- Each and every one of
us is doing what we can.

00:09:16.692 --> 00:09:18.581
- It's the fact that I
have a great ICU team.

00:09:18.581 --> 00:09:20.700
I have the best ICU nurses in the world.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.690
- The unity, the compassion, and empathy.

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:26.560
- Humanity exists, and
we're all in this together.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.100
- I live in New York City,
and every night at 7:00,

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.970
the entire city breaks
out in cheer and applause

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:33.350
for all the healthcare workers.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:37.350
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:39.960
- I'm hearing from families who are having

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:42.310
more family meals, more family meetings,

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.070
they're playing board games,
they're communicating,

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:44.903
they're talking.

00:09:44.903 --> 00:09:48.270
- People are coming together,
and they are helping

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:50.020
out their neighbors.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:53.560
- Letters like this in my
mailbox from my neighbor,

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.260
spreading love across this country.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.520
- Every patient that I called,

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:59.060
the first thing they
asked is how was I doing.

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:01.040
- The outpouring of love and support

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:02.900
from communities all around the world,

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:05.550
showing their support for
healthcare workers, like me,

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:06.460
on the frontline.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.520
- All of our frontline
workers, in hundreds of roles,

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.570
inside the hospital and outside of it,

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.460
working their tails off every single day.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.790
- My trainees all stepping up to volunteer

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:16.780
to help in the ICU.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.930
- Healthcare professionals
everywhere are stepping up

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:19.970
instead of backing down.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.390
- The emergency department
staff, now more than ever.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.400
- We've put aside all turf wars

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:25.980
and inter-departmental bickering.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.460
- The fact that the world
has set aside its differences

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:31.320
to work on novel treatments, vaccines,

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:32.630
and drugs for this virus.

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:34.590
- The people donating and making supplies.

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:36.950
- Like when we see businesses
that stop their work

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:39.490
and start producing equipment
for healthcare providers.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.910
- Even famous fashion
designers, like Chanel

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.786
and Christian Siriano are
making masks and gowns.

00:10:44.786 --> 00:10:46.800
- The numbers are getting better.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:48.160
Prevention does work.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.240
- Seeing people on their
balconies applauding those

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.970
on the frontline gives me hope.

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.870
And seeing science
working, creating vaccines,

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:56.540
creating treatments is what gives me hope.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.890
- I'm fighting for the hope
that one day, very soon,

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.801
we overcome this, that we
get back to normal life

00:11:01.801 --> 00:11:04.620
and don't take the small
things for granted again.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:06.180
- And you know what gives me hope?

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.170
The fact that I was able to get over 100

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:11.320
of my physician colleagues
to make this video for you.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:13.520
I usually sign off my videos by saying

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:15.140
stay happy and healthy.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.340
But for this one, let's
do something different.

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:20.140
Stay alert, not anxious.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:21.807
- [Everyone] Alert, not anxious.

00:11:23.069 --> 00:11:24.652
Alert, not anxious.

00:11:26.102 --> 00:11:27.685
Alert, not anxious.

